yeah we understand that the prime  minister will resign today look i spoke  to a cabinet minister this morning who  had seen the prime minister had a long  conversation with him yesterday and said  to the prime minister the game is up you  simply do not have the numbers uh to  fill posts in your government the  country will be ungovernable you cannot  carry on uh he tried to hold on last  night you saw the reports  on the news but as we understand it this  morning let me just get the statement up  from on my phone uh that boris johnson  we understand has spoken to the tory uh  party chair or committee chair 22 chair  graeme brady and agreed to stand down so  we're going to expect a resignation for  from boris johnson later today it's over  for him he tried until the very end to  hold on but when you're faced with over  50 government resignations half a dozen  of your cabinet walking out and finding  yourself unable to fill even cabinet  positions with ministers uh i'm willing  to be promoted with parliamentarians  unwilling to serve  that's when your government collapses  the game is up for boris johnson he's  going to have to stand down  okay beth so  what happens  no unprecedented times the helicopters  are already up the street has gone  absolutely bonkers what happens tonight  well what we will expect to happen now  is the prime minister will be in there  this morning he will be with his  advisers he will be drafting a  resignation statement  and we'll expect to hear from him later  that will then of course trigger  a leadership race within the  conservative party and i think what is  difficult about this one compared to the  moment that theresa may resigned in 2019  was back in 2019  there was a clear  successor to tresemme it was boris  johnson and he went on to win that  leadership race and a runoff against  jeremy hunt but this time  the field is wide open  politicians are not ousting boris  johnson because of a policy policy  disagreement as they did over may  regarding brexit and they don't really  have a plan of what comes next or who  they would like to be leader they are  literally ousting him because they  cannot serve under him and it's just got  too bad being in a boris  johnson cabinet government and even  parliamentary party and so what will  happen now is he will resign and then  there will be a leadership contest and  in the coming days we will see all the  runners and riders coming out to make  their pitch  to the parliamentary party we've already  had overnight sawela bravo man she's the  attorney general the most senior legal  mind in government  she has  announced overnight that she uh would  like uh to run  we've got rishi sunak we've got sajid  javid we've got tom tuggenheart the  chair of the foreign affairs select  committee who is perhaps the favored  choice of the one nation group of  conservatives in the party what about  brandon lewis the northern ireland  secretary that just resigned nadim  zahari penny morden i have got such a  long list of would-be runners and riders  and then we're going to have a  competition uh to see who uh takes the  job but it comes at such a difficult  time  for the country given the cost of living  crisis and the difficulties that  households up and down the land  have are having and i've just got an  official number 10 statement just out  the prime minister will make a statement  to the country today so boris johnson  will make a statement today it is over  for him he won the biggest majority  didn't he back in 2019 of any  conservative prime minister since  margaret thatcher he was potentially a  two-term president uh prime minister but  after two and a half years uh his reign  has come to an end and boris johnson is  standing down as conservative party  leader and prime minister  well it's the moment in history again  beth isn't it you've witnessed so many  for us already as our political editor  um  when do you think we will hear from him  when will he make that statement and in  what capacity do we know yet  i don't know yet kay what i do know is  as i've said there is now an official  statement  saying that boris johnson will make a  statement to the country later  and as i was saying earlier he has  spoken to sir graham brady who went to  see him yesterday the chair of the 22  back bench committee and agreed to stand  down as a party leader so a new leader  can be in place by party conference so  that is in october  at the end of september into october a  new party leader in place uh for the  autumn summer  he will remain prime minister until that  point so i've just been told by a number  10 figure the prime minister is now  agreeing to an orderly handover of power  so instead of fighting on he's now  agreed to resign he's told brian brady  of his intentions and he will remain  prime minister over the summer while  that leadership race is played out  and they hope to have a new prime  minister and conservative party leader  by the autumn so  the summer recess is going to be taken  up by a lot of campaigning by would-be  new prime ministers and conservative  party leaders is such an incredible  moment  we could see really  as i was saying a couple of days ago  that his time was up when those  resignations happened in cabinet that  was perhaps the moment  and then the snowball in effect over the  12 hours following when dozens of  government resignations began  to fall in and cabinet members then went  didn't they yesterday in a delegation to  tell boris johnson he had to go but even  last night number 10 were briefing of  his defiance telling me that he was  going to call sir gray and brady's bluff  that he was going to force a confidence  vote in him well overnight and as dawn  broke and more people resigned brandon  lewis standing down as northern ireland  secretary and then nadim sahari telling  the prime minister that he had to go  and then we had michelle donald also the  education secretary the game up for  boris johnson however hard he fought  however much he wanted it it was simply  not tenable for him to continue

